Statuses describe the experimental deliverables, not readiness for clinical use.
These are the exact success-criterion sentences extracted from the supplied DOCX.

Additional gaps: free-text symptom exploration is not implemented; the suggested
`notebooks/06_model_evaluation.ipynb` is absent (evaluation exists as tested modules
and saved artifacts); the hypothesis dashboard omits the omnibus statistic; and
prediction CSV names use `probability_low`/`probability_moderate`/`probability_high`/
`probability_critical` rather than the case-study sketch's reversed naming. Clinical
validation is **not met** and is a prerequisite to any clinical use. The case study
sets no numerical performance acceptance threshold, so passing software criteria
must not be described as meeting a clinical accuracy or recall target.

